However, the heterogeneity of mobile devices presents a significant challenge. Devices vary in terms of sensing capabilities, battery life, and computational power. Consequently, a single device may not be able to complete all assigned tasks within the required time limits. To mitigate this issue, we propose a new framework for mobile crowdsensing that exploits device heterogeneity to enhance task completion rates. This framework employs a task allocation strategy that assigns tasks to devices based on their specific capabilities. Additionally, we develop a task scheduling algorithm that prioritizes tasks with tighter deadlines to maximize the number of completed tasks. We also present a distributed algorithm to solve the task scheduling problem. Finally, extensive simulations demonstrate that our proposed framework and algorithm outperform existing methods.

