\section{Introduction}
Reinforcement learning (RL) has become a prominent area of research, with numerous algorithms developed to address diverse problems. However, RL faces significant challenges, particularly the curse of dimensionality, which hinders its ability to learn effectively in high-dimensional state spaces. This paper proposes a solution to this issue by combining a pre-trained neural network with an RL agent. The pre-trained network is trained on a dataset derived from a simulator, while the RL agent learns from the same environment. We illustrate that this combined approach surpasses the performance of either the pre-trained network or the RL agent used in isolation. Additionally, we demonstrate that the method is compatible with various RL algorithms, such as Q-learning, SARSA, and DQN. Finally, we confirm the method's efficacy using a real-world dataset. The source code can be found at https://github.com/abhishek1234567890/RL_with_pretrained_network.

